Q1) Eloquent basics (10 marks)

1)Explain $fillable, $guarded and $hidden in one line each.

$fillable is used to define the mass assignable fields/attributes. 
$guarded is used to define the fields/attributes which are only required, mostly you should use either fillable or guarded.
$hidden is used to define the fields which should not show in the request. 


2) A form sends an extra field is_admin=1 that is not in $fillable. What happens with Employee::create($request->all())? Why is $request->validated() safer?
if the field/attribute is_admin is not in the $fillable in the model file then when trying to create the employee will $request->all() will still save the data. $request->validated() is used instead in order to first validate the data according to the set of rules written in the http/request which is called in this controller function. If the validation fails laravel will throw an error.

3)Why cast joining_date to date? What do you get back with and without the cast?
We cast the value of joining_date to date because we only want to store the date instead of date and time and in order to make to easily show to he frontend.

