How many queries does this run for 50 employees, and why?

  this would run and solve the n+1 query probelm if we use eager loading and use - with or load.
  without it query runs 50 + 1 times

2)Rewrite the controller query so the number of queries stays fixed.
public function index(Request $request)
    {
        $query = Employee::with('department', 'projects');

        if ($request->user()->hasRole('employee')) {
            $query->where('user_id', $request->user()->id);
        }

        $employees = $query->paginate(10);

        return view('employee.index', [
            'employees' => $employees
        ]);
    }

3)What is the difference between with() and load()?

with() is used to get the relationshipwise data while we are building the query 
load() is used when we already have the model returning the data and want to modify the existing query further. 

