You added a new Spatie permission but users still get 403. What is the likely cause and the fix?
Policy as applicable throughout the program and cannot be manipulated unlike blade and the drawback in blade is that you have to keep managing the same rule across all the new forms which are going to be created. 403 status code stands for unauthorized that means the user has not been assigned the permisson even they though they may have been assigned a role. you need to check the roles ->  then permissons assigned to that roles and also cross verify is the correct role is assigned to the user. if all this is correct then check if the correct middleware permisson logic is written on the route in the web.php or api.php route files.




